      <Comment source="PMN, nilo-poyanco, kothari, SRI">Thermospermine, an isomer of spermine, was discovered for the first time in the thermophilic bacterium |FRAME: TAX-274| |CITS: [479149]|. Later, thermospermine was also found in the halophilic archaeum |FRAME: TAX-2242|, in several species of |FRAME: TAX-357|, in |FRAME:TAX-266| and in leguminous seeds, e.g. from |FRAME: TAX-3888| and |FRAME: TAX-3908| |CITS: [17560575]|.</Comment>
